From: Ubuntu Desktop bug work
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: Harden Ubuntu overview search providers

The Web Search Provider and Snap Search Provider extensions reach into
gnome-shell private SearchResults APIs. Combined with silent parental-
controls refusal and lock-screen enable/disable, that:

  * unregisters a provider that was never registered, which on
    gnome-shell before 50.1-0ubuntu1.2 splices index -1 and drops an
    arbitrary other provider (LP: #2150103, #2161808, #2156486);
  * throws against an already-disposed ListSearchResults after overview
    recreation;
  * races enable() after await getDefaultBrowser() with disable().

This patch:

  * uses the public SearchController addProvider/removeProvider API;
  * tracks whether registration actually attached a display;
  * only unregisters a provider that was registered;
  * aborts web-search enable() if disable() cancelled the Gio.Cancellable;
  * fixes SnapFinderSearchProvider.get_id throwing TypeError (LP: #2150265);
  * stops advertising the in-process snap finder as a remote provider so
    AppSystem 'installed-changed' does not drop it forever;
  * assigns the snap: URI handler before launch_uris_async.

Bug-Ubuntu: https://launchpad.net/bugs/2150103
Bug-Ubuntu: https://launchpad.net/bugs/2150265
Bug-Ubuntu: https://launchpad.net/bugs/2156486
Bug-Ubuntu: https://launchpad.net/bugs/2161808
Forwarded: no
